X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute
DTSTART:20260628T173000Z
DTEND:20260628T190000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
SUMMARY:Drop-in Tours and Crafting
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the final day of this exhibition!An Immersive Expe
 rienceInspired by Indonesia's spectacular coral reefs\, acclaimed fiber a
 rtist Mulyana (b. 1984\, Bandung\, Indonesia) invites you to wander throu
 gh a handcrafted seascape where art and ecology meet.  Explore colorful c
 oral reefs\, playful fish\, and fantastical sea creatures — all meticul
 ously hand-knit and crocheted.  Pause to reflect on the delicate balance 
 between human wellbeing and the vitality of our oceans.  Chat with a Muse
 um Guide to deepen your understanding.  Create Your Own Sea CreatureEnjoy
  a hands-on activity in the gallery.  No prior experience is needed — a
  volunteer can guide you step by step.  Choose from a fish\, octopus\, lo
 bster\, sea urchin\, or crab.  All supplies are provided\, so you can div
 e right in!  Why Visit? This exhibition is more than art — it's a livin
 g conversation about beauty\, fragility\, and our shared responsibility t
 o protect the ocean. Whether you're an art lover\, a family looking for a
  creative activity\, or simply curious\, Vital Ecosystems offers a memora
 ble experience for all ages.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us on the final day of this exhibi
 tion!</p><h4><strong>An Immersive Experience</strong></h4><ul><li>Inspire
 d by Indonesia's spectacular coral reefs\, acclaimed fiber artist Mulyana
  (b. 1984\, Bandung\, Indonesia) invites you to wander through a handcraf
 ted seascape where art and ecology meet.  </li><li>Explore colorful coral
  reefs\, playful fish\, and fantastical sea creatures — all meticulousl
 y hand-knit and crocheted.  </li><li>Pause to reflect on the delicate bal
 ance between human wellbeing and the vitality of our oceans.  </li><li>Ch
 at with a Museum Guide to deepen your understanding.  </li></ul><h4><stro
 ng>Create Your Own Sea Creature</strong></h4><ul><li>Enjoy a hands-on act
 ivity in the gallery.  </li><li>No prior experience is needed — a volun
 teer can guide you step by step.  </li><li>Choose from a fish\, octopus\,
  lobster\, sea urchin\, or crab.  </li><li>All supplies are provided\, so
  you can dive right in!  </li></ul><p><strong>Why Visit?</strong> This ex
 hibition is more than art — it's a living conversation about beauty\, f
 ragility\, and our shared responsibility to protect the ocean. Whether yo
 u're an art lover\, a family looking for a creative activity\, or simply 
 curious\, <em>Vital Ecosystems</em> offers a memorable experience for all
  ages.</p>
